{{!
    @template local_ai_course_assistant/analytics_tab_comparison

    AI vs Non-Users tab of the analytics dashboard. Replaces the innerHTML
    string that amd/src/analytics_dashboard.js used to build for this pane
    (CONTRIB-10574 #278).

    The table headings and the metric labels are still literal English, exactly
    as they were in the JavaScript this replaces.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * cards - array of stat tiles, each with a value and a label
    * rows - one entry per metric, each with metric, aival and nonval

    Example context (json):
    {
        "cards": [
            {"value": "41", "label": "AI users"},
            {"value": "87", "label": "Non-users"}
        ],
        "rows": [
            {"metric": "Avg Grade (%)", "aival": "82.4", "nonval": "74.1"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="sola-stat-cards">
    {{#cards}}
        <div class="sola-stat-card">
            <div class="sola-stat-value">{{value}}</div>
            <div class="sola-stat-label">{{label}}</div>
        </div>
    {{/cards}}
</div>
<div class="row mt-4">
    <div class="col-md-8">
        <canvas id="sola-chart-comparison" height="120"></canvas>
    </div>
</div>
<table class="table table-sm mt-4">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Metric</th>
            <th>AI Users</th>
            <th>Non-Users</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {{#rows}}
            <tr>
                <td>{{metric}}</td>
                <td>{{aival}}</td>
                <td>{{nonval}}</td>
            </tr>
        {{/rows}}
    </tbody>
</table>
